The analyzer shows the primary scorer quality_score is broken (mean ~4.815e8, out-of-range) while optimization is entirely driven by parameter_spread (mean 0.4738 ≈ max 0.5). Fixing the scorer implementation is required, but that must be done outside this controller. To reduce risk from single-objective saturation and to give the optimizer a plausible interim signal that may correlate with true quality, add parameter_mean as a modest secondary objective now (so search is not purely spread-driven). This is a low-risk, reversible objective-level change that preserves the current setup while we await a true scorer fix.

